>> On demand delivery of IT resources over the internet with pay-as-you-go model/pricing is called cloud
computing ( using IT resources with the help of internet ..servers, storage, database, softwares ).

>> VPC = Virtual Private Cloud ( our own private network in AWS

>> IP address = it's like a unique ID that is used to connect/communicate between devices over a network

>> Public IP = used to connect to internet
   Private IP = used to connect internally or internal communication between devices within our network

>> 10.0.0.0/8 = lower number means more IP address requirement and vice-versa. Each segment is of 8bits and total of
                32bits and each segment can be of 255 IPs. ( here 2^24 i.e. 16,777,216 IP addresses are needed and
                                                             we get 2 less IPs as they are taken for broadcast IP )

>> Subnet = dividing a large, single network into multiple smaller interconnected pieces

>> We create ec2 instance( server/VM ) in any of the subnets that is presented inside a VPC ( Our own network )

>> Instance type = according to our performance requirement/workload we will choose the instance type that indicates
                   about the configuration of a instance

>> INSTANCE TYPES -
                 . General purpose = for normal usecase
                 . Compute optimize = for high performance
                 . Memory optimized = for high memory/fast performance
                 . Accelerated computing = for best computing purpose like best graphic card for gaming, faster calculation
                 . Storage optimized = for fast i/o operations like read-write ops, for faster content retrieving

>> Deploying website in AWS ec2 = after creating a instance and associating it with elastic IP connect it to you system by ssh. Then
                                  go to root folder and go to var directory, there install apache server( httpd ). After this go to
                                  /www/html directory and start&enable httpd then create a html file and put your website content in
                                  it and save it. Now in instance go to security groups and edit inbound by adding rule that enables
                                  'http' and make the address 0.0.0.0/0 and save it. Finally paste the public elastic IP in the
                                  browser to see the Website.

>> Creating a Windows ec2 instance = Create a instance and choose Windows as the OS ( follow the same steps as there in creating
                                     linux instance ). Then click on connect and go to rdp client and click create password ( here
                                     upload the key-pair file that is selected while creating the instance ) and click on decrypt key                                     
                                     After this go to remote desktop connection in your pc and paste the public ip address in
                                     <computer> then in the user block enter the name as administrator and paste the password and
                                     click yes to access the ec2 windows server.


>> Accessing server that is present in private subnet connected to a private route table  by creating NAT gateway = =
                                   First create a VPC then create public subnets and private subnet and create one public route table
                                   and private route table then attach a igw and associate public subnets to the public route table.
                                   Now create a NAT gateway in public subnet and associate elastic IP and attach it then associate
                                   private subnets to private route table. Then create two ec2 servers and place one server in public                                  
                                   subnet and other in private subnet. Connect one server through ssh and save a file with the name
                                   of key-pair file.pem and paste the key's encrypted content inside that created file ( both servers                                  
                                   must have same key-pair ). Now go to that second server and connect through ssh but enter private                                   
                                   IP of hat server. Now the private subnet's server is connected by internal connection.
                                   ( private subnet's server doesn't have any public IP and if there also it has no use ).
                                   ( The key's file inside public server should be secure so do chmod 400 to the file ).
                                   ( The server in public subnet that is used to connect private server is called as jump server ).
                                   ( Public server is also called as jump server )

>> NAT gateway = It is used to connect private route table that are connected to private subnets. Its job is to translate the private             
                 IP to public IP when the request is incoming and vice versa ensuring secure,private connection.

>> Inbound = whichever the thing that is coming from the internet to the server.
>> Outbound = whichever the thing that is going from the server to the internet.

>> Security groups = protects the server
   NACL = protects subnet ( works based on priority, after creation associate it to the subnet and add inbound rule for connection )


>> VPC Peering = Establishing connection between VPCs and enabling communication is called VPC Peering.
                 for connection of VPCs the CIDR(IP) should be different and not same ( the IPs should not be same for any )

                 How to peer VPCs? >>
                 Create two VPCs ( more than two VPC peering can also be done ) and create igw,route tables,subnets,
                 NAT gateway ( if you want to peer a private server ) on both VPCs. After connecting both VPC's servers , go to
                 peering connection of one VPC  server and enter the details of the servers you want to peer then go to the peering
                 connection of another VPC server and in actions button select 'accept'. Now go to the route tables of 1st VPCs
                 server and in edit route section add rule by entering the CIDR range of 2nd VPC in both route tables and do the same           
                 for 2nd VPCs server, after this go to security groups of both server and add inbound rule of ICMP .
                 Now in both ssh connected servers perform ping <private_IP> , if it pings then the VPC peering is successful.

>> Taking a server backup = When take a ec2 server's backup it  works like a server level backup and stores it as a image in AMI
                            window. To take a image( backup ) select the server and click on actions and select image and templates
                            and enter the details then create it ,now the image( backup ) of the server is created.
                            ( if you want to delete the backup go to the AMI and select and click actions and AMI de-register after
                             this go to snapshots section and delete snapshot ).
                               There are two ways to access the backup again, one is select it in ami and click launch instance from                             
                               AMI or by simply clicking launch instamce and there in MY AMI select the AMI and launch the instance.
                               ( While accessing and creating from the servers we can change the configuration and all which is known        
                                as Vertical Scaling )
